From 5ecb95683a7e0ab5cb96c5dfe3feb430b9ca9af5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:31:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: tell the user when the TV input offers only
 Low-Latency Dolby Vision

A TV input in its game mode (on an LG, Quick Frame Transport) advertises Dolby
Vision Low-Latency only, which native output does not use: a Dolby Vision video
then plays without native output, and only the player information said why.

When a Dolby Vision video opens without native output and the display's Dolby
Vision block is a version 2 one of 12 bytes or more without the Standard
interface (CDisplayInfo::SupportsLowLatencyDolbyVisionOnly()), a notification
says so and how to get native output. It is shown once for each state of the
display: again after what native output depends on changes (not, say, the audio
formats of a sound bar behind the TV) or after a restart, not with every video
of a playlist, and not while the display's information may be old (its EDID
could not be read, or it is gone).

The text is the English core string 39999; its translations are an Estuary
string (31689: es_es, es_ar, es_mx), used only with Estuary as the skin, since
another skin may give that number another meaning (CGUIUtils::GetHadesString()).
Hades cannot add to Kodi's core translations, which are language add-ons
downloaded from Kodi's repository.
